2. Dataset leads from awesome-public-datasets (https://github.com/awesomedata/awesome-public-datasets)

   The metadata of awesome-public-datasets (its apd-core repository) is licensed under GPL-3.0, so none
   of it was copied. The homepage URLs listed there were used as leads for independent research on
   2026-09-27, and later its licence values as hints for checking licences (see below). Every field of the 613 resources whose provenance.origin is "apd-link" -- and of the
   dataset facets added to 77 existing resources -- was written from each resource's own website, under
   this registry's own inclusion rules and vocabularies; names, descriptions, domains, tags, licences
   and all other values were not taken from that project. Of the 973 leads, 613 became resources of
   their own, 77 added a dataset facet to a resource already listed, and 283 were not used (dead, no
   data, paid only, duplicates, or rejected on review).

   Later the same day, with the maintainer's approval, the `license` field of those entries was read as a
   hint for 43 resources whose licence was unknown or disputed. Each licence was checked on the resource's
   own site before use: 33 were set to what that site states (10 of them differ from the hint), 5
   existing values were confirmed, and 5 stay unknown. No licence text was taken from that project.

